  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25e-perchlike-fishes-5-remaining-cichlids-from-south-and-central-america/chaetobranchopsis_orbicularis_en/",
      "html": "<p>Origin: Brazil. Total length up to 20 cm. A plankton eater.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "beforeYouBuy",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25e-perchlike-fishes-5-remaining-cichlids-from-south-and-central-america/chaetobranchopsis_orbicularis_en/",
      "html": "<p>Chaetobranchopsis orbicularis is rarely imported, as such nutrition specialists are mostly of interest only to specialists and enthusiasts. Care is not necessarily difficult. The biggest difficulty is feeding, which can be managed with a well-functioning artemia culture. If you are willing and able to manage this, there are no obstacles to purchasing these animals.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25e-perchlike-fishes-5-remaining-cichlids-from-south-and-central-america/chaetobranchopsis_orbicularis_en/",
      "html": "<p>There are no special demands regarding water conditions or aquarium arrangement.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25e-perchlike-fishes-5-remaining-cichlids-from-south-and-central-america/chaetobranchopsis_orbicularis_en/",
      "html": "<p>Artemia are absolutely necessary, especially during the settling-in period, and must always be available as a basic food. Fish of about 15 cm need significant quantities. Later they can also be fed a balanced diet of other foods, even the smallest frozen food such as lobster eggs, cyclops or daphnia. The best is frozen artemia. Dry food is hardly accepted.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25e-perchlike-fishes-5-remaining-cichlids-from-south-and-central-america/chaetobranchopsis_orbicularis_en/",
      "html": "<p>Despite its size it is a harmless aquarium occupant, and because of its eating habits it can easily be kept with smaller fish. When kept with other cichlids, these must not be aggressive species.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25e-perchlike-fishes-5-remaining-cichlids-from-south-and-central-america/chaetobranchopsis_orbicularis_en/",
      "html": "<p>Captive breeding has not yet been successful.</p>"
    }
  ],
